# Grid: the value of Area places an item by row and column, with a span, or automatically.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Grid · Placement
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 20mm
	Section:
		Text: Grid
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Placement
		Paragraph: The value of `Area` is `row column`, counting from 1, with `rows columns` after it to span several. Without a value the item goes to the next free cell, and `auto auto 1 2` to the next free place two columns wide. An item past the last row adds rows.
			Style: intro
		Text: Area: 2 3 / Area: 1 1 / Area: 1 2 1 2 / Area: 2 1 2 1
			Style: label
		Grid:
			Column sizes: repeat(3, *)
			Row sizes: 30 30 30
			Gap: 4
			Area: 2 3
				Text: 2 3
					Style: tile
			Area: 1 1
				Text: 1 1
					Style: tile
			Area: 1 2 1 2
				Text: 1 2 1 2  (one row, two columns)
					Style: pale
			Area: 2 1 2 1
				Text: 2 1 2 1  (two rows, one column)
					Style: pale
		Text: Area:  (automatic) and Area: auto auto 1 2
			Style: label
